    "content": "Transamerica is a major American financial services company specializing in life insurance, retirement planning, savings, and investment solutions. As a subsidiary of the Netherlands-based Aegon N.V., it focuses on serving individuals and employers. Transamerica is well-known for its insurance products, annuities, and mutual funds, often marketing to the middle market. Aegon N.V. Key details about Transamerica: Core Products: They offer life insurance (term, whole, indexed universal), annuities, and investment options. life insurance annuities investment options Retirement Focus: Transamerica is a major provider of retirement plans for employers of all sizes. Parent Company: Owned by Aegon N.V. since 1999, representing their U.S. operations. Aegon N.V. Background: Founded in 1906, it was historically a conglomerate (including airlines and car rentals) but shifted focus in the 1980s exclusively to financial services. Reputation: Recognized as a top insurance provider, with strong financial stability ratings, though it has faced criticism regarding customer service in some reviews. The company is associated with the iconic Transamerica Pyramid building in San Francisco, although they no longer maintain offices there.",
